Agreed.  But sometimes it's worth a late-game cost to get an early-game
advantage (especially since by Gehennom, things are usually much less
sticky than they are pre-Castle.

e.g. it may be worth having your barbarian enhance two-handed sword or
battle axe to, say, "skilled" if that helps you survive early, even
though you know you're not going to use it later.

Be aware of the tradeoffs you're making.  But don't necessarily play to
maximize late-game studliness at the cost of not making it to the
late-game.



